  "aiOverview": {
    "content": "The Masters Green Jacket is an iconic, highly exclusive prize in sports, awarded annually to the winner of the tournament at Augusta National Golf Club. Only 1 (sometimes 2) is awarded each year, with winners holding it for a year before returning it to be kept at the club, symbolizing lifetime honorary membership.Key Details About the Green Jacket:Significance: Introduced in 1937 to identify club members, it became a, if not the, premier prize for winning the tournament.Cost & Availability: It is not for sale; the club does not make them available to the public.Who Gets One: Only tournament winners, club members, and select individuals receive one.Rules & Restrictions: The winner can take their jacket home for the first year, but after that, it must remain on the club's grounds. They are usually worn during official club activities or designated appearances.Design: It is officially \"Masters Green\" (Pantone 342) featuring a custom chest patch and brass buttons.Key Rules for Winners:The Return: The champion keeps the jacket for one year before returning it to the club.The Exclusivity: The jacket cannot be worn at just any function; they are generally restricted to official, respectful appearances, ensuring the exclusivity of the honor.Replacement: If a winner's jacket is damaged, it can be repaired or replaced by the original, official tailor, 1.For more information about the tournament's history and members, visit the Wikipedia article about the Masters Tournament.",
